      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 881,
      "costUsd": 0.007993,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a C D F from a formula. F of x is x squared over nine for x from zero to three, zero below that, and one above. Is it valid? At zero it's zero, and at three it's one, so the pieces join without a jump. Its derivative, two x over nine, is never negative there, so F never decreases. Graph it by hand or with a graphing app. It's flat at zero, leaves the origin flat, then curves up more and more steeply to the point three, one, and stays flat at one. It's not a straight line."
    },
