      "pronunciationText": "Two hundred and twenty five cuts the two hundred to two hundred and fifty class in half. Assume its one hundred and sixty masses are spread evenly, so about eighty are above two hundred and twenty five. Add the forty in the top class. That's one hundred and twenty out of four hundred, zero point three. Zero point five is wrong. It counts the whole class, including masses below two hundred and twenty five."
